     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi's teacher showed a barometer and a wind vane in the school weather corner.\n\"They read the sky,\" she said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "pressure",
     "humidity",
     "barometer"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Atmospheric pressure is the weight of air pressing on us. A barometer measures it. Low pressure often brings clouds and rain and high pressure brings clear skies.\nWind is moving air, measured with an anemometer for speed and a wind vane for direction. Humidity is the amount of water vapour in the air, measured with a hygrometer.\nWeather stations collect all these readings so forecasters can predict weather."
    }
